<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Applied when a release is signed, and only then: Tauri passes this to `codesign` alongside the
  hardened runtime, which notarization requires. An unsigned local build ignores it.

  One key, and it is the one the hardened runtime takes away silently. Without it macOS denies the
  microphone with no prompt at all, and dictation records nothing. That covers SoX's `rec` too:
  macOS charges a child process's microphone use to the responsible application, which is why
  `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription` lives in this bundle's Info.plist and not with SoX.

  Nothing else is here because nothing else is needed. wtm sends no Apple Events, loads no
  libraries but its own, and its WKWebView compiles JavaScript in WebKit's own process, so the
  JIT entitlements that Electron apps carry would only widen what a compromised wtm could do.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
